DESCRIPTION:Public Archaeology Day from 1 to 4 p.m.\nMonroe Lake: Salt Cree
 k SRA\n\nBefore Monroe Lake was built\, the Salt Creek Valley was home to 
 numerous small family farms\, some dating back to the 1820s. While most ho
 mesteads have been reclaimed by time and nature\, remnants remain in the f
 orm of scattered foundation stones\, piles of rock and brick from collapse
 d chimneys\, wells and cisterns\, and fragments of metal and pottery.\n\nA
 rchaeologists from the Indiana Division of Historic Preservation and the U
 .S. Army Corps of Engineers\, Louisville District are partnering with the 
 Indiana Division of State Parks to document some of these historic sites. 
 Members of the public can assist with mapping sites and conducting shovel 
 probes to search for artifacts or just stop by to view the work and ask qu
 estions. \n\nIf you would like to assist the archaeologists\, advance regi
 stration is encouraged by noon on Nov. 4 – but walk-up volunteers are al
 so welcome!\n\nSalt Creek SRA is located at the eastern/southern end of Mo
 nroe Dam Road in Bloomington (the eastern end of the Monroe Lake reservoir
  dam)\; entrance is free. When you arrive\, look for signs directing you t
 o the archaeological work site. Please note that the work site is not acce
 ssible\; it is located in the woods and may require walking up to 1/3-mile
  on uneven ground.
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Salt Creek State Recreation Area\, southern/eastern 
 end of Monroe Dam Road (ignore State Road 446 address)
SUMMARY:Uncovering Our Past: Public Archaeology Day\, Salt Creek SRA (Monro
 e Lake)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/uncovering-our-past-public-archae
 ology-day
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
