DTSTAMP:20260926T045221Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54028367184188
DTSTART:20261107T183000Z
DTEND:20261107T193000Z
DESCRIPTION:Elkinsville History Tour at 1:30 p.m.\n\n•    Sign up at tiny
 url.com/elkinsville2025 \n•    Registration required by November 3.\n•
     Cost is $10 per person.\n•    Limited to 15 people\; recommended for
  ages 14 and up.\n•    Location: Meet at the Story Inn parking lot in St
 ory\, IN\n\nJoin us for a tour through the “town that was!” Prior to t
 he construction of Monroe Lake\, Elkinsville was a center of commerce and 
 community for a remote part of Brown County. Explore the history of this t
 own\, walk its former main street\, visit the cemetery\, and find out what
  happened to this community after the lake went in. 2 hrs 30 min (approx.)
 \n\nAll registrations are final. No refunds will be offered\, unless the t
 our itself is cancelled. You may transfer an existing reservation to anoth
 er person by contacting Jill Vance at jvance@dnr.in.gov at least 2 days pr
 ior to the tour.
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Meets at Story Inn parking lot in Story\, IN (ignore
  S.R. 446 address\; directions will be emailed to registered attendees)
SUMMARY:Uncovering Our Past: Elkinsville History Tour (Monroe Lake)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/uncovering-our-past-elkinsville-h
 istory-tour-monroe-lake
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Monroe County Government
X-SOURCE-URL:https://events.in.gov/search/events?event_types%5B%5D=49056849667840
DTSTAMP:20260926T045221Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54028422771879
DTSTART:20261107T230000Z
DTEND:20261108T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:Southern Indiana Folk Songs at 6:00 p.m.\n\n•    Free program
  (donations accepted) and free park entry!\n•    Location: Paynetown Sta
 te Recreation Area\, Activity Center\n•    Please note that seating is l
 imited to 25 people\; we don’t expect the room to fill\, but we could al
 ways be surprised!\n\nFolk songs proliferated in an era when singing was a
  common form of recreation. People learned traditional folk songs by liste
 ning to others sing them and then passing them on to someone else. The Sal
 t Creek Valley\, where Monroe Lake now lies\, has a rich history of song\,
  heavily influenced by the people who moved here in the 1800s from the App
 alachian region. This program explores the history of folk music in southe
 rn Indiana and songs once sung right here in the valley\, including audio 
 recordings of local singers from the 1930s through 1980s.
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Paynetown SRA\, Activity Center
SUMMARY:Uncovering Our Past: Southern Indiana Folk Songs\, Paynetown SRA (M
 onroe Lake)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/uncovering-our-past-southern-indi
 ana-folk-songs-paynetown-sra-monroe-lake
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
